---
kind: quest
luteVersion: "0.9.0"
uses: ../world.schema.yaml
title: Unmoored
---

/*
  The frame quest. It becomes available at the first release — episode 3, where
  forty metres of ship stop being ship — because that is where "the ship is
  coming apart" stops being a warning and becomes a measurement.

  What this quest WANTED to say and cannot: "and the shed is still short of the
  greenhouse when the story ends". Every `done=` is evaluated continuously, so a
  hold-the-line objective (`run.shedPressure < 2`) is satisfied at activation and
  the quest completes before the player has done anything. There is no end-of-run
  evaluation point in the language, so the goal is written in its positive form
  instead — get a hand onto the coupling — and the losing side is `fail=`. See T9.4.
*/
<quest id="unmoored" title="Unmoored" start="true" fail="run.shedPressure >= 4" after="visited('anseo.s01ep03')">
<objective id="aHandAtTheCoupling" title="Have somebody aboard who can stop the shed" done="count(can_halt(_)) >= 1"/>
<objective id="somebodyToWalkWith" title="Give Vesna a reason to work with you" done="run.vesnaTrust >= 1"/>
<objective id="theOrderOnPaper" title="Get the order of release onto paper you have read" done="holds(knows(vesna, manifest))" optional/>
<on event="questComplete">
@narrator: A hand that could reach the coupling, and somebody willing to stand next to it.
</on>
<on event="questFailed">
@narrator: The schedule ran out ahead of the crew, and the ship went on subtracting itself.
</on>
</quest>
